stage: 1
finding: Blocking brief premise: stage 1 requires Shallot's native target on Dawn with no browser compositor, but crates/native exposes only system wry (WebKitGTK on Linux, explicitly documented in main.rs as having no usable WebGPU) and portable CEF/Chromium. cef_backend.rs enables browser WebGPU/Dawn features, creates a CEF browser for a page URL, and initializes renderer/GPU subprocesses; it does not provide compositor-free Dawn surface presentation. Therefore the required native comparison arm and full Check cannot be met as written with this target. CEF may be a browser-runtime comparison, not evidence excluding the browser compositor. Parent approval is needed to mark this arm unavailable and narrow the conclusion, or separately authorize a genuine compositor-free Dawn presentation harness; do not silently substitute CEF or headless Dawn.
